WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.870
Raetsel, what are we doing here?

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:19.910
This is where it ends.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.250
It’s where our journey ends, Jin.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.000
Our journey... is over?

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.200
That’s right! It ends here.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.260
Kaito!

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.370
Kaito Daimon!

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.990
The Journey Ends

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.350
Kaito!

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.500
How did you find us here?

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.000
Have you been doing well, Jin?

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.060
Yeah, of course.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.190
So you really did come, Kaito Daimon!

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.400
The POG’s investigation
network truly is impressive!

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.510
That’s not how we found you!

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.030
Enigma was the one who
told us about this place!

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.490
He’s just usin’ you!

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:54.460
And you’re lettin’ him play with you
like a cat high on silver vine!

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.380
Raetsel, I want to talk to you in private.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.030
Kaito...

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:06.910
Fine. There is something
I’d like to tell you, too.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.640
In that case, I’m gonna be the mediator!

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.850
N-Nonoha!

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.770
Kaito, you’re such a moron that you
can’t say what you mean!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.060
Now see here! This is no
time to call me a moron!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.940
But you’ll admit that you are one?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.440
Just a little!

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.180
It’s okay.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.570
It looks like you’re
special to Kaito Daimon,

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.920
so I’ll let you spend as much
time together as possible.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:39.920
Sure enough, cracking the Pythagoras Document
is proving to be a challenge!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.200
Yeah. But knowing us, we can pull it off!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.720
The Puzzle of God’s reason for existence
is shrouded in a veil of secrets!

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.700
But I swear we will solve this mystery!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.690
We will, for Kaito!

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:13.740
It was all a lie?

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.410
Yeah. Same goes for that line
about Jin hating puzzles

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.040
and how he sought the annihilation
of all puzzlers...

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.110
Enigma made all that crap up!

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.840
He was deceiving you, Jin and
all of the Master Brains.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.890
Enigma was using you to carry
out vengeance on his behalf.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.680
Even that was just a way to divert the blame.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.370
It wasn’t the puzzle’s
fault that his fiancée died!

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.260
Everything we’re telling you is the truth!

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.070
You’ve gotta believe us, Raetsel! Please!

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.140
I had already caught on.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.270
I knew that he was using me.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:56.270
And I also figured that the Jin you
believe in is probably the real one.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.960
It simply made more sense that way.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.410
Besides, I like the Jin you
described better anyway.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.030
Raetsel!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.760
What a relief!

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.340
Yeah, this was all one big
misunderstanding from the start.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.000
It was weird for you to be at

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.100
each other’s throats
when you love Jin so much!

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.210
Kaito can win her over, can’t he?

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.050
Hello?

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.460
Okay...

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:35.060
Uh-huh. All right.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:39.020
Iwashimizu, Upperclassman Jikukawa said

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.110
he wants you to send footage of us to Japan!

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.070
<i>Roger! Roger!</i>

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.570
But nothing’s going to happen.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.750
<i>Recording. Recording.</i>

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.320
After all, there’s no reason
for them to continue fighting.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>Recording. Recording.</i>

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.080
I hope yer right...

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.440
This puzzle...

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:07.800
I’ve seen it somewhere...

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.100
I won’t hand Jin over to anyone.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:25.150
I didn’t go on a journey with Jin to
help him unlock his memories,

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.160
but to keep them locked.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.970
If his memories come back,
Jin will choose you instead of me.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.620
Raetsel, what are you talking about?!

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.820
There is something I’d like to tell you.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.500
I think Jin is probably on the verge
of recovering his memories.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:41.790
What?!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:57.730
Not bad...

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:04.020
As expected from a puzzle created
by the Phi-Brain, Jin Makata.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.730
Jin has been acting strange.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:11.700
It only lasts for a second,
but every now and then,

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.880
he turns into someone neither of us knows.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.530
What’re you talking about?

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.090
I’m scared!

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:20.020
If he’s the real Jin...

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.970
But I don’t care if he is!

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.050
Raetsel...

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.290
As things stand now,
I bet Jin’s memories would flood back

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.550
if we did something big to trigger them.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.210
The Killing Coliseum will be the trigger.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:38.710
That’s the puzzle.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:44.550
It’s one of the last puzzles
Jin and I designed together.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.510
He told me, “I want to build it someday.”

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:55.420
This is a sentimental puzzle for Jin,
so if we use the one I built...

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:00.400
as the grounds for where you
and I fight to the death...

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:02.580
Fight to the death?

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:08.010
Kaito Daimon, this is your ultimate
chance to restore Jin’s memories.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:11.100
If you win, Jin will be all yours.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.970
But even if Jin chooses you,
if you aren’t around anymore...

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:21.490
But you know Kaito wouldn’t do that!
Kaito would never steal Jin from you.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.480
Why are you saying this?!

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.710
He has you and his friends,

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.980
but I only have Jin.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.640
Jin is my everything!

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.760
Jin means more to me than he does you!

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.500
Jin-Jin!

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.680
Jin-Jin!

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:47.550
That’s right...!

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:51.740
The person who created this puzzle...

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.190
It was me!

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:56.980
What’s that?

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:59.030
The Killing Coliseum’s blueprints.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:02.020
It wouldn’t be fair if I knew
its layout and you didn’t.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:04.390
Kaito?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.650
You know, I’m getting this
really icky premonition.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.160
I’ve seen enough.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.100
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:41.360
Kaito...

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:45.930
You really are a major moron!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.780
There was no stopping them, huh?

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:23.750
Yeah. Neither of them were willing
to listen to a word we said.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.590
Kaito...

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.150
We’ve reached the point of no return.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.460
Are you ready?

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.230
Yeah.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.230
Puzzle time... Let’s begin!

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.120
Kaito! Raetsel!

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.690
Sheeit! It’s started!

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:27.910
Mr. Principal, isn’t this...?

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.930
Yes, it’s a fearsome puzzle.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.750
You must dodge around
oncoming massive iron balls

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:40.810
while racing from the bottom
of this five-story coliseum

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:42.770
to the goal at the top in this battle puzzle.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.690
There are crossroads scattered
throughout the coliseum.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:53.520
The iron balls obey one of three signals:
They will go to the right, the left,

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.870
or pass through without
altering their course.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:02.210
Each time an iron ball passes through,
the signals change automatically.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:07.050
There are crossroads that Kaito can control,

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.540
crossroads that Raetsel can control,

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.470
and crossroads that neither
of them can control.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:14.000
This means there are a total of three
different types of signs.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.970
As for the fate of the loser...

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.230
The goal will close on him.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:23.200
He will be hounded by the
iron balls until he perishes.

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:32.810
You were willing to go so far
as to create this puzzle...

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.710
I’ll never let him have Jin!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:59.210
I love Jin more than anyone else ever could!

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.730
Kaito, look out!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:16.980
Damn it!

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:45.010
It’s cruel! So terribly cruel!

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.510
It demeans humans, toying with their lives...

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.280
It’s just like the Puzzle of God!

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.780
The Puzzle of God?

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:57.490
<i>Abnormal brainwaves! Abnormal brainwaves!</i>

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:58.840
Are you all right, Jin?

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.660
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.500
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.400
I can’t!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.870
<i>Anomaly detected! Anomaly detected!</i>

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.040
I must not recover my memories!

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.830
<i>Danger! Danger!</i>

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:06.680
Gammon!

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:12.170
Yeah. Once this battle is over,
Jin will recover all of his memories.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.880
Raetsel might have known what
she was talkin’ about!

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:20.640
But for that to happen, either
Kaito or Raetsel will die...!

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.600
I, Ana, think that Kaito was able to see it.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.300
Huh?

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.560
I saw it!

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.170
I saw the future!

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:33.510
I’m going to believe in that future!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:38.310
I’m gonna free Jin and Raetsel from
Enigma’s puzzle of revenge!

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.370
We’ve almost got it, Rook.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.510
Yeah, but...

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.590
So it wasn’t just me?

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.450
What could this be?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.200
I’m filled with this sense of dread...

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.320
I’m terrified to learn what
the decryption’s results say.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.010
Kaito!

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.030
What was that about?!

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.020
Guess!

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.390
The real battle is just beginning!

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:21.770
Yeah!

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.280
It’s okay. This is for the best.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:38.790
I’ve got it! I know what
Kaito’s goin’ for!

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.260
Check that out!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:46.730
At this rate, they’ll reach
the goal at the same time!

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:48.980
The battle’s gonna end in a tie!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:51.440
You’re right!

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.720
Kaito, you bastard!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.720
This is what you
were goin’ for the whole time!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.490
Kaito...

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.570
Jin!

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:15.820
Jin!

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.040
Jin!

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.710
Enigma, you scumbag!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:30.610
Jin Makata, I shall allow you
to participate in the puzzle!

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:36.740
Behold as the two who admire you are
killed by none other than your puzzle!

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:39.220
And then follow them to Hell!

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.240
Hang tight, Jin!

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.570
Jin!

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:51.790
Kaito! Raetsel! No!

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:54.040
Stay back! Go back!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.000
The iron balls are headed straight for Jin!

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:01.300
Damn it! There’s too many of them!

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:03.870
Kaito! Raetsel!

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.070
Jin-Jin...!

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:14.770
I can’t...! I must not...

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.010
I must not unlock my memories!

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:23.990
The puzzle I created is about to
take Kaito and Raetsel’s...

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:29.750
Unacceptable! I cannot... let that happen!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:34.140
Are you watching, Lovushka?

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:37.520
In a matter of minutes, Jin Makata

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:41.060
and two of the Phi-Brain
children will go to Hell.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:46.060
This is our puzzle of revenge!

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.290
I...

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.250
I...

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.320
I...!

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:19.040
I won’t accept that future!

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:24.370
Jin!

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:25.750
Jin?!

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:39.270
Jin...

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:48.270
Kaito, Raetsel, leave the rest to me.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:51.580
I’m sorry

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:55.550
for everything I’ve put
you two through up till today.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:03.410
Jin... did you get your memories back?

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:05.660
We can talk later.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.680
This is my puzzle. I can get us out of here!

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:10.670
Let’s go!

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.260
Yeah!

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.170
Uh-huh!

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:16.670
Mr. Principal!

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.930
Jin has come back!

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:32.310
An iron ball!

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:33.690
That way!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.450
Good job, Kaito!

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.670
You’ve got it, Raetsel!

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.190
Uh-huh!

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:55.030
It’s useless!

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.350
There is nowhere to hide!

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.480
We’re almost there!

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:19.000
Great! We’re safe here.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.420
Jin, is this supposed to be a...?

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:22.490
You guessed it!

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:25.750
No matter what, the iron balls
will never reach this area.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:26.240
What?!

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.770
I designed it so that when the
contestants were in a pinch,

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:31.870
they could run here for refuge.

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:36.140
My puzzles may be harsh, but
they aren’t killer puzzles.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:40.260
I know! After all, they’re
your puzzles, Jin!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.710
And if this was made according
to my blueprints...

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:49.800
What’s that?

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:51.450
What?!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:53.720
Go on! Hurry!

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:10.180
Kaito, Raetsel...

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:11.980
This is goodbye...

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.600
Kaito!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.380
Kaito!

00:21:24.020 --> 00:21:24.940
Kaito!

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:26.400
You did it, Kaito!

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.320
Yeah!

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.030
Rae-Rae, you must be happy!

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.020
Jin Makata!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.260
Enigma!

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:40.520
You bastard! I won’t forgive
you! I’ll never forgive you!

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:41.860
Silence!

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:50.430
Who... are you?

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:53.000
This is...!

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.970
This is the truth behind
the Puzzle of God...!

00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:01.360
Kaito, no matter what, don’t
restore Jin’s memories!

00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:11.430
Jin Makata has been obliterated.

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:15.260
I possess the intellect of the gods!

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.230
I am the Phi-Brain, Orpheus.

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:23.730
He’s... Orpheus?

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:06.640
Jin’s eyes... Who exactly is this Orpheus?

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:08.310
Master Rook has issued emergency orders!

00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:09.100
Mr. Bishop?

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:10.260
We can talk later.

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:12.720
If we don’t hurry, it will be too late!

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:13.890
Understood!

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:15.870
Next time, “Become a Phi-Brain.”

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:27.980
Become a Phi-Brain

00:24:16.240 --> 00:24:19.950
Come on! We’ve got to get
our hands on some POGeye!

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:23.190
They’re cleansing, refreshing and
revitalizing for your eyes!

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:25.580
Hey, was that an advertisement...?

00:24:26.410 --> 00:24:27.040
Yes.

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Revitalizing

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
